via `find_connector()`.\n     - Uses `register_l2norm_prune_hook(connector, k_ratio, method)` and `register_random_prune_hook(connector, k_ratio, method)` functions.\n     - Model: SmolVLA with `policy.model.vlm_with_expert.vlm.model` for LLM layers\n     - Backup created at `.bak`\n\n   - **`/root/autodl-tmp/lerobot/src/lerobot/policies/pi05/modeling_pi05.py`** (SERVER, read-only reference)\n     - Key function `compute_layer_complete` (line 227): shows how attention is computed layer-by-layer with eager attention\n     - `embed_prefix` (line 641): builds [vision_tokens | language_tokens] prefix\n     - `sample_actions` (line 780): runs prefix through paligemma LM with KV caching, then iterative denoising\n     - Gemma config: 8 Q heads, 1 KV head, head_dim=256, uses `modeling_gemma.eager_attention_forward`\n\n   - **`/root/autodl-tmp/lerobot/src/lerobot/policies/smolvla/modeling_smolvla.py`** (SERVER, read-only reference)\n     - `VLAFlowMatching` class with `SmolVLMWithExpertModel`\n     - `embed_prefix` includes image special tokens, language scaling (sqrt(dim)), state projection\n     - `sample_actions` builds KV cache from prefix, then iterative denoising\n\n   - **`/root/autodl-tmp/openvla-repo/prismatic/extern/hf/modeling_prismatic.py`** (SERVER, read-only reference)\n     - `OpenVLAForActionPrediction` extends `PrismaticForConditionalGeneration`\n     - `self.projector` at line 241, `self.language_model` at line 248\n\n   - **`artifacts/patch_pi05.py`** (LOCAL - written, not yet uploaded)\n     - Patch script that modifies eval_pi05_pruning_libero.py to add attention pruning\n     - Adds `compute_attention_importance_probe` function (full text in the file)\n     - Adds `pruned_embed_prefix_attn` monkey-patch\n     - Full probe function:\n       ```python\n       def compute_attention_importance_probe(img_embs, lang_emb, lm, n_probe_layers=2):\n           \"\"\"Importance = avg attention from language tokens -> each vision token\"\"\"\n           import torch.nn.functional as F\n           from transformers.models.gemma import modeling_gemma as _gemma\n           all_vis = torch.cat(img_embs, dim=1)\n           total_vis = all_vis.shape[1]\n           full_embs = torch.cat([all_vis, lang_emb], dim=1)\n           B, S, D = full_embs.shape\n           position_ids = torch.arange(S, device=full_embs.device).unsqueeze(0).expand(B, -1)\n           hidden = full_embs\n           all_attn = []\n           with torch.no_grad():\n               for layer_idx in range(min(n_probe_layers, len(lm.layers))):\n                   layer = lm.layers[layer_idx]\n                   normed = layer.input_layernorm(hidden)\n                   head_dim = layer.self_attn.head_dim\n                   q = layer.self_attn.q_proj(normed)\n                   k = layer.self_attn.k_proj(normed)\n                   v = layer.self_attn.v_proj(normed)\n                   n_q_heads = q.shape[-1] // head_dim\n                   n_kv_heads = k.shape[-1] // head_dim\n                   q = q.view(B, S, n_q_heads, head_dim).transpose(1, 2)\n                   k = k.view(B, S, n_kv_heads, head_dim).transpose(1, 2)\n                   v = v.view(B, S, n_kv_heads, head_dim).transpose(1, 2)\n                   cos, sin = lm.rotary_emb(v, position_ids)\n                   q, k = _gemma.apply_rotary_pos_emb(q, k, cos, sin, unsqueeze_dim=1)\n                   if n_kv_heads != n_q_heads:\n                       n_rep = n_q_heads // n_kv_heads\n                       k = k.repeat_interleave(n_rep, dim=1)\n                       v = v.repeat_interleave(n_rep, dim=1)\n                   scaling = layer.self_attn.scaling\n                   attn_weights = torch.matmul(q, k.transpose(-2, -1)) * scaling\n                   attn_weights = F.softmax(attn_weights, dim=-1, dtype=torch.float32)\n                   all_attn.append(attn_weights)\n                   attn_out = torch.matmul(attn_weights.to(v.dtype), v)\n                   attn_out = attn_out.transpose(1, 2).resh